From 82afc4345e793b14ba0fd0444f0869c150d49497 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:16:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Notify the admin panel and the salon for orders,
 registration, renewal, delivery actions and booking requests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner wants the same five events on both sides: the admin panel and the
salon.

New `services/eventNotification.service.js`:

* `notifyAdmins({ title, body })` writes one `admin_notification` row with the
  internal target type `ADMINS`, which the admin panel's list now includes
  (`created_by = <admin> OR target_type = 'ADMINS'`). Salon and customer
  notification lists only ever ask for ALL / ALL_SALONS / ALL_USERS, so an
  internal event cannot leak to a partner or a customer.
* `notifySalon({ salonId, title, body, data })` writes the salon's own
  `notifications` row and pushes to every active device of that salon.
* `notifyAdminsAndSalon(...)` for the events both sides must see.

Both functions swallow and log their own failures: an order is placed, a salon
is created and a plan is renewed whether or not a notification could be
written.

Wired into:

* `shopOrder.service` — order placed, delivery partner assigned, accepted,
  rejected, and each fulfilment step (picked up / shipped / delivered);
* `razorpay/createSalonWithPlan` — new salon registration;
* `razorpay/renewSalonPlan` — subscription renewed (the copy tells the salon
  that the queue and history are open again);
* `bookingRequest/bookingRequest` — new booking request (the salon already got
  its own push + inbox row there; this adds the admin panel).

The migration `patches/migrations/2026-11-06-admin-event-notifications.sql`
adds the `ADMINS` enum value and the list index.
